      "markdown": "# _C. Finite Time Reachability_",
      "source_class": "section-header"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0007-b028",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        313.0,
        381.0,
        559.0,
        463.0
      ],
      "markdown": "The previous subsection establishes a general reachability theorem and the existence of a chain policy that realizes it. We now refine this qualitative result into a finite-time guarantee by deriving a uniform upper bound on the time required for the chain policy to drive the system to the target set. The key additional assumption is the uniform bounds on the uncontrolled hitting times:",
      "source_class": "text"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0007-b029",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        313.0,
        471.0,
        559.0,
        493.0
      ],
      "markdown": "**Assumption 8** (Upper Bound of Hitting Time) **.** _Assume that there are upper bounds of the return time:_",
      "source_class": "text"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0007-b030",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        313.0,
        498.0,
        559.0,
        534.0
      ],
      "markdown": "- _1) Return time to the support set_ Supp( _K_ ) _: ∀x satisfies H_ ( _x_ ) _∈_ [ _H_ 1 _, H_ 2] _, there exists a finite time T_ 1 _>_ 0 _,_ s _._ t _._ min _t∈_ (0 _,T_ 1] d( _ϕ_ ( _t, x,_ 0) _,_ Supp( _K_ )) = 0",
      "source_class": "list-item"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0007-b031",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        313.0,
        535.0,
        559.0,
        570.0
      ],
      "markdown": "- _2) Reaching time to the target set S_ tgt _: ∀x satisfies H_ ( _x_ ) _∈_ [ _H_ min _, H_ max] _, there exists a finite T_ 2 _>_ 0 _,_ s _._ t _._ min _t∈_ (0 _,T_ 2] d( _ϕ_ ( _t, x,_ 0) _, S_ tgt) = 0",
      "source_class": "list-item"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0007-b032",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        313.0,
        577.0,
        559.0,
        599.0
      ],
      "markdown": "Under this assumption, the maximal time needed to reach the target set can be bounded explicitly.",
      "source_class": "text"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0007-b033",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        313.0,
        608.0,
        559.0,
        665.0
      ],
      "markdown": "**Theorem 4** (Finite-Time Reachability) **.** _Let K be an assignment set satisfying the conditions of Theorem 2, and define τ_ min := min _i τi. Under Assumption 8, the time required to reach the target set from any initial state x ∈ S_ 0 _is uniformly bounded by_",
      "source_class": "text"
    },
